-- title:
--   Geometric irreducibility of the generic fibre spreads out
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, let $R$ be an integral domain which is a finite-type $k$-algebra, and let $C$ be an integral domain which is a $k$-algebra and a finite-type $R$-algebra, the $k$-algebra structures being compatible (`IsScalarTower k R C`) and the structure map $R \to C$ being injective (`FaithfulSMul R C`). Write $L = k\bigl(\operatorname{im}(R \to \operatorname{Frac}(C))\bigr)$ for the intermediate field of $\operatorname{Frac}(C)/k$ generated by the image of $R$ in $\operatorname{Frac}(C)$. Assume that $L$ is separably algebraically closed in $\operatorname{Frac}(C)$: every $\theta \in \operatorname{Frac}(C)$ whose minimal polynomial over $L$ is separable already lies in $L$. The assertion is that there exists a nonzero $r \in R$ such that for every maximal ideal $\mathfrak{n}$ of $R$ with $r \notin \mathfrak{n}$, the ideal $\mathfrak{n}C$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak{n}$ in $C$ is either the unit ideal or has prime radical.
--
--   This is the affine, closed-point form of the spreading-out theorem that geometric irreducibility of the generic fibre of a finite-type morphism over an integral base propagates to the fibres over a dense open subset (EGA IV, Théorème 9.7.7), with geometric irreducibility of the generic fibre encoded by the hypothesis that the base function field is separably algebraically closed in $\operatorname{Frac}(C)$; the conclusion says that over the open set $D(r) \subseteq \operatorname{Spec} R$ each closed fibre $\operatorname{Spec}(C/\mathfrak{n}C)$ is empty or irreducible. It is used by [`Ideal.exists_mem_and_mem_and_radical_span_singleton_isPrime`](thm.html#Ideal.exists_mem_and_mem_and_radical_span_singleton_isPrime), and its proof cites the Bertini–Noether style statement [`MvPolynomial.exists_ne_zero_and_forall_irreducible_map_of_irreducible_map_algebraicClosure`](thm.html#MvPolynomial.exists_ne_zero_and_forall_irreducible_map_of_irreducible_map_algebraicClosure), the hypersurface model [`Algebra.exists_monic_irreducible_map_algebraicClosure_hypersurfaceModel_of_forall_isSeparable`](thm.html#Algebra.exists_monic_irreducible_map_algebraicClosure_hypersurfaceModel_of_forall_isSeparable), and dimension bounds for minimal primes of fibres together with the additivity of height and Krull dimension for finite-type algebras over a field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Ideal_exists_ne_zero_and_forall_isMaximal_radical_map_isPrime.lean

import Mathlib

